Water Network Attributes Modifier – User Guide
Overview
The Attributes Modifier is a useful tool within Aquastream360 that allows you to efficiently modify multiple element attributes simultaneously. This feature streamlines network editing by enabling batch operations on junctions, tanks, reservoirs, pipes, valves, and pumps.
________________________________________
Accessing the Modifier
The Attributes Modifier dialog appears when you select “Modify Attributes” from the main application menu. This tool is designed for bulk editing operations across your water network model.
________________________________________
Interface Components
Element Selection
•	Select Element: Choose the type of network element you want to modify:
o	Pipes
o	Junctions
o	Tanks
o	Valves
o	Reservoirs
o	Pumps
________________________________________
Modification Scope
•	How do you want to modify?: Define the selection criteria for elements:
o	Modify All: Apply changes to all elements of the selected type
o	Set Condition Based on Attribute Value: Select elements meeting specific attribute conditions
o	Draw A Polygon Around Elements: Visually select elements on the network map
o	Give a List: Provide specific element names
o	Terminal Nodes / Articulation Points / Bridges: Network analysis–based selections
(available for junctions and pipes only)
________________________________________
Attribute Selection
•	Attribute To Modify: Choose which attribute you want to change for the selected elements
•	Data Type Selection: Specify the data format for input values:
o	Decimal Number
o	Whole Number
o	Text Input
________________________________________
Modification Functions
      These functions either modify the values of elements or display elements that meet the selection criteria, or show specific statistical results relevant to the selected elements.
      Function: Select the operation to perform:
o	Show: Display elements that meet the selection criteria used
o	Change to: Replace with a new value
o	Multiply / Divide / Add / Subtract: Mathematical operations that modify the current value 
o	Delete: Remove elements (with confirmation)
o	Statistical Functions: Compute mean, median, mode, standard deviation, variance
o	Power / Round: Exponential and rounding operations to modify the current value
o	Find Min / Max: Compute minimum/maximum values
________________________________________
Condition Settings (Conditional Modifications)
•	Condition: Define selection criteria when using conditional modification:
o	Equals to
o	Smaller than
o	Greater than
o	Is Not
o	Between
o	Not Between
•	Value: Specify comparison value(s)

________________________________________

Guided Input Highlights
As you work through the Attributes Modifier, the application highlights in red any fields or sections that require input based on your previous selections. This real-time guidance helps you follow the correct sequence, ensuring all necessary values are entered before applying changes. By following these visual cues, you can avoid mistakes, streamline your workflow, and confidently perform modifications across multiple elements.
________________________________________


Workflow Examples
Example 1: Batch Diameter Modification
1.	Select Pipes from Element Selection
2.	Choose Modify All from Modification Scope
3.	Select Diameter from Attribute To Modify
4.	Choose Change to from Function
5.	Enter the new diameter value
6.	Click Apply
________________________________________
Example 2: Conditional Elevation Update
1.	Select Junctions from Element Selection
2.	Choose Set Condition Based on Attribute Value
3.	Select Elevation from Attribute To Modify
4.	Set Condition to Greater than
5.	Enter threshold value (e.g., 100)
6.	Choose Add value function
7.	Enter increment value
8.	Click Apply
________________________________________
Example 3: Visual Selection via Polygon
1.	Select the desired element type.
2.	Choose Draw a Polygon Around Elements.
3.	Click Draw and Group Edit.
4.	Draw polygons on the network map to select elements. For each polygon, specify the type of elements you want to filter while drawing.
5.	Configure the attribute modifications.
6.	Apply changes. (The application allows you to apply modifications per group, enabling you to modify different attributes of multiple groups of elements in sequence.)

