Special Features
Group Editing
•	Create multiple selection groups via polygon drawing
•	The system processes each group sequentially
•	Edit group lists directly in the text field
________________________________________
Network Analysis Selections
•	Terminal Nodes: End points of network branches
•	Articulation Points: Critical junctions whose removal disconnects the network
•	Bridges: Critical pipes whose removal disconnects the network
________________________________________
Data Type Awareness
The system automatically validates input based on attribute data types:
•	Numerical attributes accept decimal or whole numbers
•	Text attributes accept string input
•	Special attributes (patterns, curves) provide dropdown selection
________________________________________
Best Practices
1.	Preview selections using the Show function before modifying
2.	Back up your network before performing bulk deletions
3.	Verify conditions with small test selections first
4.	Use statistical functions to analyze attribute distributions quickly
5.	Group similar operations into a single editing session
________________________________________
Safety Features
•	Confirmation dialogs for critical operations (such as deletion)
•	Value validation based on attribute data types
•	Clear error messages with line-number references
•	Undo protection warns about unsaved modifications
________________________________________
Troubleshooting
Common Issues and Solutions
1. “No elements meet selection criteria”
•	Verify the selected element type
•	Check condition values against attribute data types
•	Confirm element names are correct when using lists
2. Value conversion errors
•	Ensure correct data type (decimal vs. whole number)
•	Use Text Input for string-based attributes
•	Verify special values (True / False / None / OPEN / CLOSED)
3. Function not available
•	Some functions are attribute-specific
•	Text attributes usually support only Change to
•	Pattern and curve attributes require dropdown selection
________________________________________
Efficiency Tips
•	Use Modify All for global changes
•	Apply conditional filters for targeted edits
•	Use polygon selection for spatial grouping
•	Chain multiple operations without closing the dialog
•	Save frequently used element lists for reuse

